message: "If you use this harness or its findings, please cite it as below."
title: "One Flag and Two Gaps: What Zero-Shot COCO-to-Driving Detection Results Hide"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rajendran
    given-names: Adithya
    affiliation: San José State University
repository-code: "https://github.com/Adithya-Rajendran/HW1-2D-Detection"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-02"
keywords:
  - object detection
  - domain shift
  - KITTI
  - nuImages
  - YOLO26
  - RT-DETR
  - non-maximum suppression
  - Jetson Orin Nano
abstract: >-
  A devkit-faithful, tested harness for zero-shot and fine-tuned 2D detection across COCO, KITTI and nuImages,
  with paired bootstrap tests, a typed error census and Jetson Orin Nano latency. Finds that Ultralytics'
  multi-label NMS setting decides the NMS vs. NMS-free comparison on KITTI, and that the COCO-to-KITTI gap splits
  into a far-field part fixed by resolution and a near-field part fixed by fine-tuning.
